Learning inventory management is a large part of game skill.
What to put down, what to keep, knowing that the vast majority
of items are to be set down?

I tend to enter a level unburdened.  I pick up almost all items as I
go in the early game and often until well into the deeper levels.
Except I learn certain items to leave - loadstones, statues and
so on.  Once Burdened I go near the down stairs and drop many
items.  When I've explored an entire level I decide if my stash
comes down.  Either I pick up until burdened and shuttle up to
my stash or I go up their and shuttle them down.

The general principle is the current level is the most dangerous
so rarely allow myself to be burdened.  Already explored levels
have been cleared out and they generally create weaker monsters
slowly enough that i can handle them burdened.  Always be ready
to drop lots when entering battle.


